.TH "tangsible-template" "1" "2026-09-25" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tangsible-template - debug a Jinja2 template against real inventory hosts
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtangsible template\fR \fIpath\fR [\fIhostSpec\fR] [\fIansible-playbook args\fR .\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBtemplate\fR renders \fIpath\fR through Ansible'\&s templating engine by generating a playbook that templates it via a \fBansible.\&builtin.\&template\fR task, showing one tab per rendered host plus a shared \fBSource\fR tab.\&
.PP
\fIhostSpec\fR is a comma-separated list of tokens, each either a literal hostname, an inventory group name, or the special keyword \fBall\fR (every host in the inventory) - mixing them freely is fine, the result is just their deduplicated union.\& If \fIhostSpec\fR is omitted entirely, the first host reported by \fBansible-inventory --list\fR is used.\& If resolution produces more hosts than the \fBtemplate_hosts_max\fR config setting (default 10, see \fBtangsible\fR(1)), you'\&re asked to confirm before rendering against all of them.\& Extra variables can be supplied with \fB-e\fR, same as any \fBansible-playbook\fR invocation.\& If \fIpath\fR lives in a role'\&s conventional \fBtemplates/\fR directory, that role'\&s own \fBdefaults/main.\&yml\fR and \fBvars/main.\&yml\fR are made available automatically.\&
.PP
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.PP
\fBTab / Shift-Tab\fR
.RS 4
Switch tabs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBUp / Down, Page Up / Down, CTRL-B / F, Home/End, CTRL-A / E\fR
.RS 4
Scroll the active tab.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBe\fR
.RS 4
Edit the Jinja2 template file, then re-render every open host tab.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBh\fR
.RS 4
Open the "change host" dialog: type a new hostname, Enter to re-render just that tab against it - or switch to it if already open - Esc to cancel.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB/\fR
.RS 4
Search the active tab'\&s text.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBy\fR
.RS 4
Copy the active tab'\&s content to the clipboard.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBn / N\fR
.RS 4
Jump to the next / previous match when search is active.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEsc\fR
.RS 4
Close search or host dialog.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBq / Ctrl-C\fR
.RS 4
Quit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Normal exit, however the view was closed - also returned if you decline the "render against N hosts?\&" confirmation prompt.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
\fIpath\fR couldn'\&t be read, a token in \fIhostSpec\fR wasn'\&t a known host or group, no host could be resolved from the inventory, or a scratch file this view depends on internally couldn'\&t be created.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB2\fR
.RS 4
Usage error: no \fIpath\fR was given.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR(1), \fBtangsible-host\fR(1)
